{"title":"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2:_Shortcut_with_right_triangles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2: Shortcut with right triangles</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd9a3fa3a414e936336f52d443eaf7a88700e3e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-10, -4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> and has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Another circle has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d906dea9f7181d8d225705494ff4fda235ef4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fb48234e755a407618d6906fdfe1040800225a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. The line passing through the two points of intersection of the two circles has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44ea3216d3cb6a8de6ab1597b92e573f02bd1acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/3759a30b166ce3611cfc045159e579d71a25be31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{13}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"409\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rTiwXJ4M2ZI\">https://youtu.be/rTiwXJ4M2ZI</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equations of the two circles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fbf29b76951436aab3ec381878ed88a3277700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+10)^2+(y+4)^2=169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c26242f5fd48ac76bc73ed0ff5b6a7e6f720da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-3)^2+(y-9)^2=65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"19\" />. Rearrange them to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2ec7cc81156480b4063c1f70f0b292a3b4a31fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+10)^2+(y+4)^2-169=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/903fd3449b3adc7119186d8f86fff98a8f147ff3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-3)^2+(y-9)^2-65=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"19\" />, respectively. Their intersection points are where these two equations gain equality. The two points lie on the line with the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d840c7b14905a5c4803c76fe0713fcb831d9c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+10)^2+(y+4)^2-169=(x-3)^2+(y-9)^2-65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"418\" height=\"19\" />. We can simplify this like the following. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958ac2028bdaa9058b93126772c303678f561567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+10)^2+(y+4)^2-169=(x-3)^2+(y-9)^2-65 \\rightarrow (x^2+20x+100)+(y^2+8y+16)-(x^2-6x+9)-(y^2-18y+81)=104 \\rightarrow 26x+26y+26=104 \\rightarrow 26x+26y=78 \\rightarrow x+y=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"1049\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/116926a9361f70e7f543c14e1f23e4be91ef50a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"87\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by TheUltimate123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2:_Shortcut_with_right_triangles\">Solution 2: Shortcut with right triangles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2: Shortcut with right triangles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note the specificity of the radii, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fb48234e755a407618d6906fdfe1040800225a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, and that specificity is often deliberately added to simplify the solution to a problem.\n</p><p>One may recognize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as the hypotenuse of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/481e0f2720d510ab3f1ea8f9042837e257ae06cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{5-12-13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> right triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fb48234e755a407618d6906fdfe1040800225a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> as the hypotenuse of the right triangle with legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can suppose that the legs of these triangles connect the circles' centers to their intersection along the gridlines of the plane.\n</p><p>If we suspect that one of the intersections lies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units to the right of and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units above the center of the first circle, we find the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30dd9899db04c5f89432ab50fc919187420f0e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-10 + 12,-4 + 5) = (2,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />, which is in fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit to the left of and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units below the center of the second circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd0851e6c382a436dde70b469bb214ec9cc2137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6bb1c456d71ee24e7a0ee603d226a7992e5da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a859acebdd07c34704648be45c0daf108e2a29d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/45055d0f57c70f8ffed12e42c57f5fb546ba9bd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 2 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"153\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>A similar solution uses the other intersection point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/b/2ab2fdfad0ad8c934758d113f39d2509e197b890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5,8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that we simply need to find a single point on the line. Then let us choose the point on the segment between the two points. Notice that the distance between centers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/402672765f1dd4a6553e350702dfb0617bd25c75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, and since the point of interest is on the radical axis we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6788ab1509a19e6e07297c210a3e5005df0bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-13^2=(13\\sqrt2 -x)^2-65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"24\" />, where x represents the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995307ce3935d1315b75f4c1f9cfbcf6a4b0b425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-10,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a321100840d97bb5e3b6c5d8b09c0147a127eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{17\\sqrt2}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"43\" />, so it must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/58970bf73f8b6330a3e9196ef598f7716f52ac13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> units up and right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/2303eadbcd89f1cb8a57bff5fbf446761d6e68e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-10,-4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />. This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b70665670e353b7f08193de1a4e4ebd674251cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1.5, 4.5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612dd005061b65928c17969e4e11f44e6c62a746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />\n~benjamintontungtungtungsahur\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B\">2017 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221417\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 298/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2296/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7352/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.785      1 -total\n 60.02%    7.674      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.18%    4.882      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15458:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221417 and revision id 289612. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}